"""Share the queue upsert between the enqueue trigger functions.

Six trigger functions each carried their own copies of the statement that queues a search projection
or Discord sync request and restarts the request already queued for the same resource. Two helper
functions now hold those statements, and the trigger functions call them.

The fan-out branches that refresh vote sessions and starboard entries used to leave a queued request's
action unchanged. They now set it to `refresh`. Those branches only select rows that still exist, and a
queued `delete` is only written when its row is deleted, so the stored result is the same.
"""

from alembic_utils.pg_function import PGFunction

from alembic import op

